    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 211920\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n1115 AM PST Sat Nov 21 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* Minimal weather impacts through next week. \n\n* A weak disturbance will bring a few showers to northern areas \n  later Sunday through Monday, including a couple of inches of snow \n  over the Sierras.\n\n* Building ridge with steady warming Tuesday through next weekend, \n  pushing above normal by Thanksgiving. Saturday could be well above \n  normal. \n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...\nWeak high pressure aloft will maintain cool and calm conditions \nthrough Sunday morning. A short-wave trough will move through the \nregion later Sunday through Monday. High chances for light rain and \nsnow over the Sierra. Elevations above 4,500 feet should see a few \ninches of snow, with a dusting down to 3,500 feet. While the chances \nare low, cannot discount a light shower or two anywhere north of Las \nVegas. Southwest winds will also increase over the mountains and \nwestern Mohave with gusts of 25 to 35 mph common. Wind advisories \nare unlikely. High pressure aloft will steadily build after and \ntemperatures will rise as a result. Expecting warming each day \nTuesday through Saturday, going above normal by Thanksgiving. \nTemperatures could push 10 degrees above normal by Saturday. Looking \nfor a pattern change the following week with multiple chances of \nrain and gusty winds. \n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 18Z Forecast Package...Winds\nwill shift to the east early in the forecast period, with some \nvariability in direction between 060-100 true. Wind speeds will \nremain under 8KT, with winds expected to generally follow typical \ndaily directional patterns, shifting to the west-southwest this \nevening and to the east again on Sunday. Increasing mid-level and\nhigh clouds are expected this evening, with bases at or above \n15kft. VFR conditions prevail.\n\n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast\nCalifornia...For the 18Z Forecast Package...Winds across much of\nthe region will remain light, under 10KT, and follow typical \ndaily directional patterns with some variability. The main \nexceptions to this are KIFP and KEED in the Lower Colorado River \nValley, where terrain-enhanced gusts to 15-20KT are possible this \nafternoon, especially at KIFP. Mid-level and high clouds will \nexpand across the region from west to east this afternoon and \ntonight, though bases are expected to remain at or above 15kft\nwith VFR conditions prevailing.\n\n&&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...RK\nAVIATION...Phillipson\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
